  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (4 of 4).\n\nThe tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They check matching versions, non-matching versions, and invalid input, using the examples from the spec. The invalid-input cases (bad versions, bad ranges, non-string arguments) all return `false` without throwing.\n\n- **Spec gaps:** where the spec is silent, I made these choices:\n  - An empty set between `||` means any version.\n  - `>*` and `<*` match nothing.\n  - Prerelease identifiers that are numeric may have leading zeros, because the spec only restricts their characters.\n  - A prerelease on a wildcard range such as `1.2.x-beta` is invalid.\n- **Number size:** numbers are parsed as `BigInt`, so very large version numbers compare correctly.\n- **Initial failure:** the first test run failed on `1.2.x-beta` being accepted. I fixed the parser to reject it.",
